{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"abbdb19966ae73c4","name":"card_unit_507th_pir","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/USA/Legions/units/card_unit_507th_pir","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"507th PIR","text":"At the end of your turn, give a random friendly infantry unit +2 attack.","flavorText":"The 507th Parachute Infantry Regiment was an airborne regiment of the US Army. The regiment was formed in 1942 and during WWII it was a unit of the 82nd Airborne Division, and later the 17th Airborne Division. The regiment was shipped to Britain in 1943 where they started to train and prepare for the invasion of Normandy that was scheduled the year after. In June 1944, during D-Day, the 507th participated in the airborne landings in Normandy and were tasked with securing the Merderet River crossings. After the successful Allied landings in Normandy the regiment continued fighting in France until early 1945. Finally the 507th participated in Operation Varsity with the 17th Airborne Division, the airborne crossing the Rhine and the largest airborne operation in history. The regiment continued fighting with the 17th Airborne Division in Germany until the war ended in May 1945.","faction":"USA","type":"infantry","rarity":"Unique","cost":2,"operationCost":1,"attack":2,"defense":3},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_507th_pir","title":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_507th_pir_title","SourceString":"507th PIR","LocalizedString":"507th PIR"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":2,"defense":3,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::USA","kredits":2,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_507th_pir_text","SourceString":"At the end of your turn, give a random friendly infantry unit +2 attack.","LocalizedString":"At the end of your turn, give a random friendly infantry unit +2 attack."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_507th_pir_history","SourceString":"The 507th Parachute Infantry Regiment was an airborne regiment of the US Army. The regiment was formed in 1942 and during WWII it was a unit of the 82nd Airborne Division, and later the 17th Airborne Division. The regiment was shipped to Britain in 1943 where they started to train and prepare for the invasion of Normandy that was scheduled the year after. In June 1944, during D-Day, the 507th participated in the airborne landings in Normandy and were tasked with securing the Merderet River crossings. After the successful Allied landings in Normandy the regiment continued fighting in France until early 1945. Finally the 507th participated in Operation Varsity with the 17th Airborne Division, the airborne crossing the Rhine and the largest airborne operation in history. The regiment continued fighting with the 17th Airborne Division in Germany until the war ended in May 1945.","LocalizedString":"The 507th Parachute Infantry Regiment was an airborne regiment of the US Army. The regiment was formed in 1942 and during WWII it was a unit of the 82nd Airborne Division, and later the 17th Airborne Division. The regiment was shipped to Britain in 1943 where they started to train and prepare for the invasion of Normandy that was scheduled the year after. In June 1944, during D-Day, the 507th participated in the airborne landings in Normandy and were tasked with securing the Merderet River crossings. After the successful Allied landings in Normandy the regiment continued fighting in France until early 1945. Finally the 507th participated in Operation Varsity with the 17th Airborne Division, the airborne crossing the Rhine and the largest airborne operation in history. The regiment continued fighting with the 17th Airborne Division in Germany until the war ended in May 1945."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Unique","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Legions","returnSet":"ECardSetEnum::OceaniaStorm","showBoostIcon":true,"EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Trigger","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnEndOfTurn"],"extraHelpTextBubbl